  [{ name := "RLV-1 path space",
      reason :=
        "A path space for curves in a manifold, with the compactness (Arzela-Ascoli) or convexity argument that produces a minimiser of the L-length. The layer works with an explicit admissible-path structure instead; existence for the general interface is state-only." },
    { name := "RLV-2 L-geodesic equation",
      reason :=
        "The first variation of the L-length, the resulting L-geodesic ODE, and its solvability. Only the finite-dimensional Gaussian model has an explicit geodesic here." },
    { name := "RLV-3 minimiser regularity",
      reason :=
        "Regularity of a minimiser (smooth on (0, tau], continuous at the base time) and the endpoint value l(0, tau) = 0. No variational regularity theory is available." },
    { name := "RLV-4 L-exponential map",
      reason :=
        "The L-exponential map based at (p, 0), its differentiability and the Jacobian used in the Jacobian comparison. The map is not constructed." },
    { name := "RLV-5 second variation and index form",
      reason :=
        "The second variation of the L-length, the L-index form and its nonnegativity along a minimiser. This is the input to both Jacobian comparison and the differential inequality for l." },
    { name := "RLV-6 Jacobian comparison",
      reason :=
        "Perelman's Jacobian comparison: the Jacobian of the L-exponential map is bounded above by the Gaussian comparison Jacobian under a Ricci curvature lower bound. Stated here as a Prop." },
    { name := "RLV-7 reduced-length differential inequality",
      reason :=
        "The inequality l_tau - Delta l + |grad l|^2 - R + n/(2 tau) >= 0 satisfied by the reduced length, with its Laplacian, gradient and scalar curvature terms. The layer keeps the surviving consequence l' >= -n/(2 tau) as the field `derivative_lower` of the Gaussian density certificate." },
    { name := "RLV-8 differentiation under the integral",
      reason :=
        "Dominated convergence / differentiation under the integral sign for the reduced volume integral, producing the derivative sign from the pointwise inequality. The certificate takes the derivative as data." },
    { name := "RLV-9 manifold metric flow",
      reason :=
        "Smooth Riemannian metrics on a closed manifold, the manifold Ricci tensor, the covariant derivative calculus and bounded curvature. Inherited from the blocked Poincare.D7.Curvature layer; the pinned mathlib has no manifold Ricci flow." },
    { name := "RLV-10 Gaussian normalisation",
      reason :=
        "The normalisation integral of the Gaussian weight, (4 pi tau)^{-n/2} times the integral of exp(-|x|^2/(4 tau)), equal to one. Not needed for the finite-dimensional computation of the reduced length in the Gaussian model, but needed for the reduced volume normalisation." }]
